    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green (**30 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**), including the new `Cp19Tests` daily-limit checkpoint.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nA new \"daily owner limit\" rule on `POST /api/owners`: if 100 or more owners already have today's `registrationDate`, the request is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests**.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing per-city capacity rule):\n\n- **`EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws a checked `DailyOwnerLimitException` once the count reaches 100.\n- **`DailyOwnerLimitException`** \u2014 checked escalation carrying the current count.\n- **`DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `429` with `{\"errors\":[\"dailyLimit\"]}`.\n- **`escalation/\u2026DailyOwnerLimitException.yml`** \u2014 routes the escalation to the handler.\n- Wired a new `dailyLimit` step into `owners.POST.yml` (after the city-capacity check, under `govern: [ transaction ]`).\n\nThe step counts *existing* owners dated today, so the 101st create in a day is the one rejected \u2014 exactly what `Cp19Tests` asserts (create 100, then the next is 429).",
